      ],
      "in_summary": true,
      "summary_section": "PREAMBLE"
    },
    {
      "sentence_id": 7,
      "text": "It was a case instituted upon a police report in which after full-fledged trial, the learned CJM acquitted the accused respondent from the charges under Sections 420, 467, 468 and 471 of the IPC.",
      "rhetorical_role": "PREAMBLE",
      "start": 669,
      "end": 864,
      "entities": [
        {
          "text": "Sections 420",
          "label": "PROVISION",
          "start": 822,
          "end": 834
        },
        {
          "text": "467",
          "label": "PROVISION",
          "start": 836,
          "end": 839
        },
        {
          "text": "468",
          "label": "PROVISION",
          "start": 841,
          "end": 844
        },
        {
          "text": "471",
          "label": "PROVISION",
          "start": 849,
          "end": 852
        },
        {
          "text": "IPC",
          "label": "STATUTE",
          "start": 860,
          "end": 863
        }
      ],
      "in_summary": true,
      "summary_section": "PREAMBLE"
    },
    {
      "sentence_id": 8,
      "text": "As per the proviso to Section 372 of the CrPC, the appeal would lie before the Sessions Judge,\nJaisalmer.",
      "rhetorical_role": "PREAMBLE",
      "start": 865,
      "end": 971,
      "entities": [
        {
          "text": "Section 372",
          "label": "PROVISION",
          "start": 888,
          "end": 899
        },
        {
          "text": "CrPC",
          "label": "STATUTE",
          "start": 907,
          "end": 911
        },
        {
          "text": "Sessions Judge,\nJaisalmer",
          "label": "COURT",
          "start": 945,
          "end": 970
        }
      ],
      "in_summary": true,
      "summary_section": "PREAMBLE"
    },
    {
      "sentence_id": 9,
      "text": "An appeal does not lie before this court.",
      "rhetorical_role": "RPC",
      "start": 972,
      "end": 1013,
      "entities": [],
      "in_summary": true,
      "summary_section": "decision",
      "summary_sent_score": 0.3329004645347595
    },
    {
      "sentence_id": 10,
      "text": "If it had been a criminal case instituted upon a private complaint, then sub-clause (4) of Section 378 of the IPC would attract and then the complainant would have to file a leave to appeal, but that is not the case here.",
      "rhetorical_role": "PREAMBLE",
      "start": 1014,
      "end": 1235,
      "entities": [
        {
          "text": "sub-clause (4) of Section 378",
          "label": "PROVISION",
          "start": 1087,
          "end": 1116
        },
        {
          "text": "IPC",
          "label": "STATUTE",
          "start": 1124,
          "end": 1127
        }
      ],
      "in_summary": true,
      "summary_section": "PREAMBLE"
    },
    {
      "sentence_id": 11,
      "text": "Accordingly, the instant leave to appeal is dismissed.",
      "rhetorical_role": "RPC",
      "start": 1236,
      "end": 1290,
      "entities": [],
      "in_summary": true,
      "summary_section": "decision",
      "summary_sent_score": 0.3596492111682892
    },
